  "description": "Subject: Overview of the \u201cCustomer Support Workflow\u201d Configuration  \n\nThe\u202fCustomer Support Workflow\u202fis an active (enabled) automation designed to process incoming support tickets. Its purpose is to route tickets efficiently to the right agents. A webhook trigger named **newTicket** (created by admin) listens at\u202fhttps://example.com/webhook/ticket\u202fand forwards each incoming ticket to two parallel branches: **node1** and **node2**.\u202fNode\u202f1 is a **filter** that checks the condition\u202f`priority == 'high'`; it is labelled \u201cHigh priority filter\u201d and, when the condition matches, passes the ticket to **node3**.\u202fNode\u202f2 is an **assign** step that sets the\u202fassignee\u202fto\u202fsupport_team\u202fand also forwards the ticket to **node3**.\u202fNode\u202f3 is a **notification** action that sends an email using the template\u202fticketAlert; its metadata records that the notification was sent at\u202f2026\u201106\u201115T12:00:00Z. This final node has no further outputs.\n\nGlobal variables used by the workflow are defined as follows: the key\u202f**default_priority** holds the JSON string\u202f\"\\\"medium\\\"\"\u202f(i.e., the string \u201cmedium\u201d), and the key\u202f**max_retry_count** holds the JSON value\u202f3. The workflow description reads: \u201cAutomated workflow to handle incoming support tickets and route them to appropriate agents.\u201d"
